# starter_01 — THE NARROWS
#
# BACKLOG A2.  ⚠ This is the SOURCE; `maps/starter_01.json` +
# `maps/starter_01_markers.json` beside it are BUILT from it by
# `scripts/build_maps.sh` and are what `make play MAP=starter_01` loads.
# `tests/a2_the_maps.loft` asserts the two still agree.
#
# ⚠ It is also playable directly, without building:
#     make play SCRIPT=maps/starter_01.keys
#
# ⚠⚠ A map holds the GROUND and the MARKERS and nothing else.  A `crew`
# or a `schedule` line here would be authored, played, and then silently
# dropped by the save — the run's wave list is the seven-wave default
# every `PlayState` starts with (`waves.loft::wave_list_default`).
#
# One way in, five hexes wide, walled with a firing lane down the middle.
# The first base: it teaches WHERE TO STAND, and nothing else.
echo starter_01: the narrows — one way in, and it is five hexes wide

at 0 0 1

# ── The ground.  Unpainted is SEA, so the paint IS the geometry. ──
palette 5

# The home field, west.
drag   -9  -7    4  -7
drag   -9  -6    4  -6
drag   -9  -5    4  -5
drag   -9  -4    4  -4
drag   -9  -3    4  -3
drag   -9  -2    4  -2
drag   -9  -1    4  -1
drag   -9   0    4   0
drag   -9   1    4   1
drag   -9   2    4   2
drag   -9   3    4   3
drag   -9   4    4   4
drag   -9   5    4   5
drag   -9   6    4   6
drag   -9   7    4   7

# The neck — the only way through, five rows wide.
drag    5  -2    9  -2
drag    5  -1    9  -1
drag    5   0    9   0
drag    5   1    9   1
drag    5   2    9   2

# The approach field, east, where the robots form up.
drag   10  -7   24  -7
drag   10  -6   24  -6
drag   10  -5   24  -5
drag   10  -4   24  -4
drag   10  -3   24  -3
drag   10  -2   24  -2
drag   10  -1   24  -1
drag   10   0   24   0
drag   10   1   24   1
drag   10   2   24   2
drag   10   3   24   3
drag   10   4   24   4
drag   10   5   24   5
drag   10   6   24   6
drag   10   7   24   7

# ── The wall across the neck, with (7, 0) left open. ──
#
# ⚠ The gap is the TOWERS' firing lane, not an oversight: a `wall` is
# 3 m and blocks a sight line, so a fully sealed neck would leave both
# towers looking at masonry.  `plans/12` B7 measured a gate as worth
# nothing to the WALL; it is worth everything to the guns.
palette 9
click    7  -2
click    7  -1
click    7   1
click    7   2

# ── The markers ──
do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click    0   0
marker   0   0 target

# Two towers on the lane, one behind the other.  Park BETWEEN them at
# (4, 0) and one vehicle repairs both — measured at +52 ticks and a
# whole extra wave over parking at the core (`@M045`).
do cycle_kind
click    3   0
click    5   0
marker   3   0 tower
marker   5   0 tower

# The spawn, facing home.
#
# ⚠⚠ TWENTY-TWO hexes out, and the number is DERIVED: a tower reaches
# 15 (`TOWER_RANGE_HEXES`) and the forward one stands at (5, 0), so a
# spawn inside q = 21 is one the towers SHELL AS IT ARRIVES — wave 1
# then dies without ever walking, and the neck this map is built
# around never gets used.  The floor is 12 (`WAVE_1_PROVOCATION_HEXES`)
# and the ceiling is the drive home in front of them.
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click   22   0
marker  22   0 spawn 3

do toggle_mode

count markers 4 4
kind 0 0 grass
kind 7 0 grass
kind 7 1 wall
kind 12 5 grass
